# What is git push?
- git push uploads local commits to the remote repository, such as GitHub

           Local(laptop/computer) -----> Remote(Git Hub rrepo)

# command :
git push origin main

Where:
origin = remote repository name
main = branch name


 ############# QUICK RIVISION ############### 

# Clone repository
git clone <repository-url>

# Check status
git status

# Stage a file
git add <file>

# Stage everything
git add .

# Commit changes
git commit -m "message"

# Push to GitHub
git push origin main

# Pull latest changes
git pull origin main
